The tick hands the processor on without putting the preempted thread back on its queue.
The thread would stay ready and never run again;
every ready thread but the running one that may run waits on a queue.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a ready thread that may run waits on no queue

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -630,9 +630,7 @@ static void turn_end(void)
     uint32_t offset = turn_close();
     struct thread *was = turn;
     turn = NULL;
-    if (was != NULL) {
-        thread_settle(was);
-    }
+    (void)was;
     turn = next_turn(offset);
     run_turn();
 }
